  ### Controls and exact assertions

  - Start prints exactly:
    ```text
    UNIT=<unit>
    DIR=<jobdir>
    WAIT=bash <absolute-launch.sh-path> wait <jobdir>
    ```
  - Verified exact systemd arguments:
    ```text
    --user
    --collect
    --unit=<unit>
    --property=MemoryMax=8G
    --property=TasksMax=1024
    --property=RuntimeMaxSec=7
    --property=WorkingDirectory=<caller-directory>
    --setenv=PATH=<PATH>
    --setenv=HOME=<HOME>
    ```
    Overrides were also asserted as `--property=MemoryMax=2G` and `--property=TasksMax=17`.
  - Successful job: `wait` and `status` return 0 and print `JOB <unit> ENDED status=0`. `wait` prints exactly log lines `line-6` through `line-45`, the last 40 lines; `status` prints only the state line.
  - Exit-3 job: both return 3; `wait` prints exactly:
    ```text
    JOB <unit> ENDED status=3
    failed
    ```
    The attempts file contains exactly one line, proving no retry.
  - Lost unit returns 125 and prints exactly:
    ```text
    JOB <unit> ENDED without a status (killed, timed out or OOM): killed
    ```
  - Deadline overrun, using one-second runtime/grace/poll test settings, returns 124 and prints exactly:
    ```text
    JOB <unit> STILL RUNNING past its deadline
    ```
    Before the deadline, non-waiting `status` prints `JOB <unit> RUNNING`.
  - Invalid `bad/name`, zero SECS, and non-numeric SECS return 2 with no stdout and clear NAME/SECS errors.
  - Missing `systemd-run` returns 2 with no stdout and exactly:
    ```text
    launch.sh: systemd-run --user is unavailable (systemd-run not found)
    ```
  - Also verified `cmd`, `unit`, numeric `deadline`, caller working directory, complete `out.log`, atomic status cleanup, executable syntax, and empty `bash -n` output.

